{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1512321-nameless-order-high-guild","id":1512321,"title":"Nameless Order: High Guild","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-21T18:28:44-07:00","id":1512321,"title":"Nameless Order: High Guild","content":"<span style=\"font-size:36px\">The High Guild</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:28px\">Power is Magical.</span><br /> <br /> <i>Why haven't we joined the worthless followers of the exarchs? I get that a lot, it doesn't even offend me anymore.<br /> It's because the followers of Mammon and the others don't understand what wealth and power are about, power in all of its forms is not a tool or an end, it's Both. Power is a bulwark against pain, those who decry us and equate us with the Ministries don't understand how many of us simply want to feel safe. All of that are some of the reasons we are never going to join the Seers. But those aren't the main reasons, the main reason is that in the end the Seers are not truly seers, they are the servants of the throne. They are servants, they scrape and beg at someone else's feet. I will not serve<br /> And neither will you</i><br /> <br /> The High Guild is just that, a guild of mages of the highest echelon. Universally wealthy and powerful in sleeper spheres, they refuse to abandon the comfort and access their Sleeper power allows them, even in Awakening. They want to have the cake and eat it too, they want to be the most powerful mages they and the most powerful people as well. And as such,they work on all levels of society to find magic in the ways of power.<br /> <br /> <b>Mages Join The High Guild </b>When they have great wealth and power, or the members of the High Guild see fit to offer both of them as an enticement to joining.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Core Beliefs: Hail to the King.</span></b><br /> <br /> A Mage is not someone who accepts less than he deserves, a mage never will bow down and scrape. A Mage is a king, but all but the Wisest have forgotten that the first Kings were not of hereditary lines,but gained their positions because they're worthy. A Mage must do the same,he must work for his Power,that's why Power is Magical.<br /> And like all magic it should be used responsibly, the High Guild believes in Noblesse Oblige, they've been given a mission to those below them and they will see it fit, and they will reap the rewards<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Balance is Necessary:</b></span><br /> <br /> Accumulating wealth. and power is a good thing, but you should understand that empathy for your fellows matters as well. The Exarchs got their chance at Ascension because we didn't respect each other's rights and property, by respecting that we weaken them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Remove Power from the Unworthy</b></span><br /> <br /> You'd be surprised how popular Robin Hood is among the High Guild, they don't see Hood so much as an anti-capitalistic figure but as someone who took wealth and power from those who used it unwisely.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Caucus</span></b><br /> <br /> The Caucus of the High Guild hides behind companies and other enterprises. They are interconnected and sometimes indistinguishable from the sleeper halls of power. Thus those places' hierarchies are used<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Mysteries</span></b><br /> <br /> The High Guild seeks mysteries with practical use, Mysteries that will enrich them in some way shape, or form. When they find a half-ephemeral guru in the woods, they seek to learn from it. When the gold of a lost hoar is cursed, they seek to lift the curse<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magical Symbolism: Aurum and the Perfected Self</b></span><br /> <br /> The High Guild believes in the<br /> Aurum or gold was the symbol and ideal that alchemists and their ilk used to symbolize perfection, the High Guild goes one step beyond and believes in the Perfected Self, a powerful idealized human being and mage both. To achieve that ideal that is both literal and metaphorical. They use the highest, most expensive, and most materials in their casting<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Hubris</b></span><br /> <br /> Greed is a sin for a reason, and they all have a shade of it. To avoid hubris, the High Guild remembers that there's no self-made man, then that's a lie made by the Exarchs. And that it should be cast down, lest they reach beyond their grasp<br /> <br /> <b>Concepts</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rapper: </b>Gold flows, and the highest lines of clothing fall. The rhymes inspired by the Tuatha de Dannaan are the greatest on the charts.<br /> <br /> <b>Stereotypes:\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow: </b>Struggles must be directed<br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium: </b>Knowledge is power, <i>all </i>knowledge<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians of the Veil: </b>Have a little more faith, ain't nothing that fragile<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Ladder: </b>You must climb to the top but shouldn't stay there.<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne: </b>I've seen delusion, and you guys go way beyond deluded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 05-22-2023, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T20:29:19-07:00","id":1512673,"title":"","content":"Interesting, so they are likely to recruit from mages later down their career ? If so, what kind of dynamic exists between recruits and their other Order ? Are they members of both, do they need to surrender membership to join the High Guild ? If not, how are conflicts of interests between both Orders handled ?<br /> <br /> What benefits do initiates receive from the Mystery Cult Initiation ? What is within their specialty for purposes of requisitioning ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T21:11:09-07:00","id":1512677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1512321-nameless-order-high-guild?p=1512673#post1512673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, so they are likely to recruit from mages later down their career ? If so, what kind of dynamic exists between recruits and their other Order ? Are they members of both, do they need to surrender membership to join the High Guild ? If not, how are conflicts of interests between both Orders handled ?<br /> <br /> What benefits do initiates receive from the Mystery Cult Initiation ? What is within their specialty for purposes of requisitioning ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your interest. Here's your answers in order<br /> <br /> They often recruit mages who already have been Awakened for a while. But they also offer sleeper money and sleeper status for those who need to encourage joining.<br /> It's difficult to be a member of the High Guild and another Order. But not impossible by any means. Conflicts of interest unfortunately have too many variables for me to give a general answer.<br /> They Receive the &quot;Searching for Perfection&quot; Order Merit. Members can requisit certain artifacts and imbued items. They own surprising number of Demesne and Verges for the a Order of their size","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T21:13:53-07:00","id":1512678,"title":"","content":"P.SThe Searching for Perfection Merit allows them to,once a week, treat any Perfected Item as a +5 Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}